Subject: [PATCH] clock: derive software adjtime progress from elapsed time

Requirement: reliable bounded wall-clock slew with coherent reads, progress
queries, replacement and cancellation, without adjusting monotonic time.

Project reads and commits from the same raw elapsed counter at 500 ppm, retaining
fractional nanosecond budget. Validate adjustment conversion and clock arithmetic,
return normalized signed timeval fields, and commit prior progress before query
or replacement. Return software clock failures through the public get/set APIs;
a failed software set must not update the RTC. Admit the software backend through
CLOCK_ADJTIME while retaining its default-disabled configuration and symbol gate.

Upstream status: local fix for the pinned NuttX 13.1.1 revision
4268617f28ad0ed7e900a081ea1b33c9347458b3; not submitted upstream.
Removal condition: select an upstream revision with equivalent behavior and pass
the retained native and target regressions without this patch.

The deterministic regression compiles the actual old/new clock sources with
mechanical host timer stubs and UBSan. Target/emulator execution and physical
RTC/suspend behavior are separate qualification gates.

